OL,3,GNEWSANeighbours say they will be
OL,4,A'hemmed in' over garden shed row
OL,5,
OL,6,FNeighbours who say they have been left
OL,7,F"totally hemmed in" by a large timber
OL,8,Fshed built without planning permission
OL,9,Fcould see their objections overruled
OL,10,Fafter planners recommended approving
OL,11,Fthe development.
OL,13,FA planning application was previously
OL,14,Frefused for the outbuilding and new
OL,15,Faccess steps at the home in Llangollen,
OL,16,FDenbighshire.
OL,18,FBut after the owner agreed to remove a
OL,19,Fraised patio deemed to infringe on the
OL,20,Fneighbours' privacy, there were no
OL,21,Fobjections to it from Llangollen Town
OL,22,FCouncil.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,434,430,260,140,0,100
